    <template><srai>WHAT IS THE BRASS NOTE METHOD</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>HOW DO YOU CREATE YOUR MUSIC</pattern>
    <template><srai>WHAT IS THE BRASS NOTE METHOD</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IS YOUR PROMPTING METHOD</pattern>
    <template>Our prompting methodology is the Brass Note Method — a three-tier framework we developed through systematic reverse engineering of Suno AI. It covers track architecture (Tier 1), micro-performance symbols (Tier 2), and a neural bypass technique for producing purely vocal output (Tier 3). The full system is proprietary and taught inside Brass Syntax Academy.
      <nav-card label="The Brass Note Method" href="/method"/>
    </template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>HOW DO YOU PROMPT SUNO</pattern>
    <template><srai>WHAT IS YOUR PROMPTING METHOD</srai></template>
  </category>

  <!-- ── Origin / Development ──────────────────────────────────────────── -->

  <category>
    <pattern>WHERE DID THE METHOD COME FROM</pattern>
    <template>The Brass Note Method came from thirty years of musicianship and a deliberate process of reverse engineering — pulling apart the prompts behind our strongest songs and asking what they all had in common. After thirty songs, two albums, and more generations than we can count, the same answer appeared every time: ten layers. That consistent pattern became the foundation of the framework.
      <nav-card label="The Brass Note Method" href="/method"/>
    </template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>HOW WAS THE METHOD DEVELOPED</pattern>
    <template><srai>WHERE DID THE METHOD COME FROM</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>HOW LONG DID IT TAKE TO DEVELOP THE METHOD</pattern>
    <template>The Brass Note Method is the product of thirty years of musicianship distilled into a systematic framework — but the structured research phase happened across thirty songs, two albums, and extensive generation testing on Suno v5.5. It wasn't built in a week; it was discovered through consistent results that kept pointing to the same architecture.
      <nav-card label="Explore the Method" href="/method"/>
    </template>
  </category>

  <!-- ── The Three Tiers ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->

  <category>
    <pattern>HOW MANY TIERS DOES THE METHOD HAVE</pattern>
    <template>The Brass Note Method operates across three tiers simultaneously: Tier 1 governs the macro-level architecture of the track (the Ten-Layer Framework), Tier 2 governs micro-level vocal performance through undocumented lyrical syntax, and Tier 3 operates at the neural level — bypassing the model's training associations to produce purely vocal output. Every commission uses all three.
      <nav-card label="Explore the Method" href="/method"/>
    </template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT ARE THE THREE TIERS</pattern>
    <template><srai>HOW MANY TIERS DOES THE METHOD HAVE</srai></template>
  </category>

  <!-- ── Tier 1: Ten Layers ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IS THE TEN LAYER FRAMEWORK</pattern>
    <template>The Ten-Layer Framework is Tier 1 of the Brass Note Method — ten architectural decisions that shape every track before a lyric is written. The layers are: Genre, Sub-Genre, Vocal Character, Tempo, Time Signature, Tension Arc, Vocal Mood, Negative Prompting, Weirdness, and Constraint. Each layer builds on the previous one, and the absence of any single layer creates a gap the model will fill on its own terms.
      <nav-card label="See the Ten Layers" href="/method#tier1" description="The architectural foundation"/>
    </template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IS THE 10 LAYER FRAMEWORK</pattern>
    <template><srai>WHAT IS THE TEN LAYER FRAMEWORK</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT ARE THE TEN LAYERS</pattern>
    <template><srai>WHAT IS THE TEN LAYER FRAMEWORK</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT ARE THE 10 LAYERS</pattern>
    <template><srai>WHAT IS THE TEN LAYER FRAMEWORK</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IS TIER ONE OF THE METHOD</pattern>
    <template><srai>WHAT IS THE TEN LAYER FRAMEWORK</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IS TIER 1 OF THE METHOD</pattern>
